  "goodToKnow": "Der Proviant is provisions, food and drink taken on a trip, hike or expedition: Proviant einpacken, der Proviant geht zur Neige (is running out). The word comes from Italian. Synonyms: die Verpflegung, die Wegzehrung (food for the journey, old-fashioned). For a hiking snack, Bavarians say die Brotzeit and Austrians die Jause. It has no plural."
